.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-COMPOSE 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-skel 0.2.88" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-compose \- turn the Right Alt Compose key on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-compose
.RB [ on | off | toggle | status ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-compose
makes the Right Alt key a Compose key, or turns it back into a normal Alt
key.
It is the
.B Compose key
entry in
.BR paperweight\-settings (1),
which shows whether it is on or off.
.PP
With the Compose key on, press and release Right Alt, then type a short
sequence to get a character that is not on the keyboard:
.PP
.RS
.TS
l l.
o c	\(co
r o	\(rg
e \(aq	\['e]
\- \- .	\(en
\- \- \-	\(em
o o	\(de
.TE
.RE
.PP
The order of the two letters matters: Compose, c, O gives \(lqǑ\(rq, not
\(co.
The full list of sequences is in
.IR /usr/share/X11/locale/en_US.UTF\-8/Compose .
.PP
The Compose key is off by default.
On keyboard layouts such as German or French, Right Alt is AltGr, which
those layouts need for characters like @ and \(Eu; turning on the Compose
key takes that away.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B toggle
Turn it on if it is off, off if it is on.
This is the default.
.TP
.B on
Turn it on.
.TP
.B off
Turn it off.
.TP
.B status
Print
.B on
or
.BR off .
.PP
.BR on ,
.B off
and
.B toggle
reload sway so the change applies at once.
Run outside a sway session, they only update the file and the change
applies the next time sway starts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/60\-compose.conf
Present while the Compose key is on; written by
.B on
and deleted by
.BR off .
The toggle only manages Right Alt
.RB ( compose:ralt ).
To use a different key, such as Right Ctrl, leave the toggle off and put
.B xkb_options compose:rctrl
(or another option from
.BR xkeyboard\-config (7))
in an
.B input type:keyboard
block in a fragment of your own, with a different file name.
.TP
.I ~/.XCompose
Your own sequences.
Start it with
.B include \(dq%L\(dq
to keep the standard ones.
See
.BR Compose (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight\-settings (1),
.BR paperweight\-keys (1),
.BR Compose (5),
.BR sway\-input (5),
.BR xkeyboard\-config (7)
